# Netlify redirect + rewrite rules for visualsbyjoshua.com
# Rules are evaluated top to bottom; the first match wins.
# A trailing "!" forces the rule even when a real file exists at that path,
# which is what makes the _private blocks effective on a drag-and-drop deploy.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal working material must never be served.
# _private/ holds audit documents, build scripts, unpublished client originals,
# and Lightroom exports. Without the force flag Netlify would serve the files
# directly, because they are present in the deploy.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/_private/*            /404.html   404!
/_private              /404.html   404!

# CLAUDE.md has to stay at the repo root for tooling, so it is blocked by path
# instead of being moved.
/CLAUDE.md             /404.html   404!
/claude.md             /404.html   404!

# Belt and braces: block the internal file extensions and names that were
# publicly reachable before this change, in case any copy reappears at the root.
/*.bak                 /404.html   404!
/ACTION-PLAN.md        /404.html   404!
/FULL-AUDIT-REPORT.md  /404.html   404!
/SEO-REPORT.html       /404.html   404!
/seo-report            /404.html   404!
/seo-audit.js          /404.html   404!
/seo-audit-report.md   /404.html   404!
/blog-gap-report.md    /404.html   404!
/skills-lock.json      /404.html   404!
/photography-blog-instructions.md  /404.html  404!

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Retired URLs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Long-standing misspelling of the testimonials page. Previously handled by a
# meta-refresh stub, now a real 301 so link equity consolidates.
/Tesimonials.html      /testimonials   301!
/tesimonials           /testimonials   301!

# Legacy extension form of the gallery page; canonical is /gallery.
/gallery.html          /gallery        301!
